jobs.description:
I’m turning Nanos World into a fully featured One Piece role-playing experience and am looking for a developer, technical artist, or combat animator who already feels comfortable working with Unreal Engine 5.7.4, Niagara, and multiplayer combat systems.

The project is built around exploration, character progression, customisation, and fluid PvP combat. The goal is to create a playable game mode that captures the spirit of Oda’s universe while remaining coherent with Nanos World’s workflow and technical limitations.

What I’m looking for

I’m looking for one or more freelancers who can help create and integrate:

• Combat animations and M1 attack chains;
• Character fighting styles;
• Kessen, based on iconic One Piece characters;
• Devil Fruit abilities;
• Dial abilities;
• Niagara VFX, projectiles, impacts, and ability effects;
• Animation/VFX synchronization;
• Hitboxes, attack timing, cooldowns, and gameplay feedback;
• Clean and readable combat effects designed specifically for PvP.

The project includes several combat categories:

• Main Arts / fighting styles;
• Kessen;
• Devil Fruits;
• Dials.

The objective is not simply to create visually impressive spells. Every ability must feel responsive, enjoyable, readable, and balanced in a multiplayer PvP environment.

PvP-first combat design

This is primarily a PvP game mode, not a PvE-focused project.

Abilities should therefore be designed around:

• Fast and responsive activation;
• Clear anticipation and impact;
• Reasonable recovery times;
• Counterplay and dodge opportunities;
• Readable hitboxes and attack ranges;
• Smooth combos;
• Good movement and positioning;
• Clear visual feedback for both the user and the opponent.

I do not want abilities that take 10 or 15 seconds to charge or play out unless there is a very specific gameplay reason and sufficient counterplay. Even high-rarity or ultimate abilities should remain enjoyable and practical to use during a real fight.

A powerful ability should feel powerful without making the combat unfair or removing the importance of player skill.

Combat categories

Main Arts

Players will be able to choose between several main fighting styles:

• Swordsman;
• Black Leg;
• Clima-Tact;
• Sniper / Marksman, available through whitelist.

Each Main Art will contain 10 combat abilities with the following rarity distribution:

• 1 E-rank ability;
• 2 D-rank abilities;
• 2 C-rank abilities;
• 2 B-rank abilities;
• 2 A-rank abilities;
• 1 S-rank ability.

Each Main Art must also have its own M1 attack chain.

M1 attacks should feel like a real combo rather than a single animation repeated indefinitely. Depending on the style, a chain could include four to six different attacks, with variations in movement, timing, range, and impact.

For example, a Sniper M1 chain could include:

• A single shot;
• Two quick consecutive shots;
• A moving shot;
• A close-range weapon strike;
• A stronger finishing shot.

Each fighting style should have a distinct identity and feel completely different to play.

Kessen

Kessen are special combat styles inspired by non-Devil-Fruit characters from the One Piece universe.

The initial Kessen roster includes:

• Mihawk;
• Oden;
• Shanks;
• Garp;
• Zoro;
• Ryuma;
• Usopp;
• Ben Beckman;
• Brook;
• Nami;
• Kin’emon;
• Arlong;
• Inuarashi.

Each Kessen will contain:

• 1 D-rank ability;
• 1 C-rank ability;
• 2 B-rank abilities;
• 1 A-rank ability;
• 1 S-rank ability.

Each Kessen should have a strong character identity. The animations, effects, movement, attack patterns, and gameplay should immediately communicate which character the player is using.

For example:

• Mihawk should focus on precise sword techniques and powerful ranged slashes;
• Garp should focus on heavy punches, shockwaves, and physical impact;
• Brook should reflect his swordsmanship, speed, and musical/soul-related identity;
• Nami should use Clima-Tact-based techniques;
• Shanks should feel extremely rare, powerful, precise, and Haki-oriented.

The goal is not to create generic abilities with different colours. Each Kessen should feel like a complete and recognizable fighting style.

Kessen rarity and balance

There should be a noticeable difference between a common Kessen, such as Arlong, and a legendary Kessen, such as Shanks.

However, this difference must remain balanced for PvP.

Higher-rarity Kessen may offer:

• Better pressure;
• More effective combos;
• Stronger mobility;
• Better range or utility;
• More impactful abilities;
• More impressive animations and VFX;
• More unique mechanics.

They should not become impossible to defeat.

A skilled player using a common Kessen should still be able to defeat a player using a legendary Kessen through better positioning, timing, reactions, and decision-making.

Rarity should enhance the experience, not replace player skill.

Devil Fruits

Devil Fruit abilities will be obtainable through gameplay.

The first development phase should focus on iconic fruits that can be created primarily through animations, projectiles, materials, and Niagara VFX without requiring complex transformation models.

Potential examples include:

• Fire;
• Ice;
• Magma;
• Light;
• Lightning;
• Smoke;
• Sand;
• Darkness;
• Rubber;
• Poison;
• Strings;
• and other recognizable Devil Fruits from the series.

The abilities should remain faithful to the visual identity and known techniques of the One Piece universe.

For the initial version, priority should be given to fruits that do not require:

• Complex character transformations;
• New full-body character models;
• Advanced deformation systems;
• Extensive custom rigging.

More complex Zoan, Ancient Zoan, and Mythical Zoan fruits may be developed later.

Dials

Dials will be obtained through an in-game reroll system. A player can equip only one Dial at a time.

The initial Dial distribution will be:

• 2 D-rank Dials;
• 2 C-rank Dials;
• 1 B-rank Dial;
• 2 A-rank Dials;
• 2 S-rank Dials.

Each Dial must have a distinct purpose and gameplay identity.

We do not want every Dial to be a variation of the same explosion with different damage values.

Possible directions include:

• Impact Dial: knockback and damage;
• Jet Dial: forward movement or dash;
• Water Dial: slowing or control zone;
• Flame Dial: short-range or ranged fire attack;
• Flash Dial: temporary visual disruption or blind effect;
• Breath Dial: directional pushback;
• Vortex-style Dial: area pull or crowd control;
• Reject Dial: powerful explosion with a meaningful drawback.

If the S-rank Dial is based on the Reject Dial and creates a large explosion, other high-rank Dials should use completely different mechanics rather than simply creating another, larger explosion.

Higher rarity should improve gameplay value, uniqueness, and presentation, not only the size of the visual effect.

Animation and VFX requirements

Each ability should be treated as a complete gameplay package.

Depending on the ability, the expected result may include:

• Character animation;
• Anticipation;
• Activation effect;
• Movement or attack animation;
• Projectile or main effect;
• Impact effect;
• Hit reaction or feedback;
• Recovery animation;
• Hitbox or area-of-effect setup;
• Timing and gameplay integration.

The ideal structure is:

Anticipation → Activation → Movement → Impact → Recovery

The animation and VFX must be synchronized carefully. A beautiful animation with poorly timed effects will not feel polished, and a good VFX effect without a convincing animation will not feel impactful.

Existing assets and packs

It is not necessary to create every animation or VFX asset from scratch.

Using existing assets is completely acceptable, including:

• Unreal Engine animation packs;
• Niagara VFX packs;
• Existing project assets;
• Modified or recoloured effects;
• Combined assets from multiple packs;
• Existing animations adapted to fit a specific ability.

The priority is the final result.

If an existing animation fits the character and ability, and is properly integrated with the VFX and gameplay, there is no need to recreate it from scratch.

The same applies to VFX.

However, all assets must be legally usable in the project, and their licenses must allow commercial use and integration into the final game mode.

Visual direction

The visual style should be strongly inspired by One Piece while remaining readable in a multiplayer game.

Effects should be:

• Dynamic;
• Clean;
• Colourful;
• Exaggerated where appropriate;
• Easy to understand during combat;
• Consistent with the character or fighting style;
• Visually distinct according to rarity.

E- and D-rank abilities can be simple and efficient.

C- and B-rank abilities should have more identity and visual development.

A-rank abilities should feel powerful and polished.

S-rank abilities should feel like signature or ultimate techniques, with a strong visual payoff, while still remaining practical and balanced for PvP.

An S-rank ability does not need to last 15 seconds to feel impressive. A short, well-timed, impactful ability is preferable to a long cinematic that removes control from the player.

PvP readability

Players must be able to understand:

• When an ability starts;
• Where it is going;
• Its approximate range;
• When it can hit;
• When it ends;
• When it may be possible to dodge or counter it.

Effects should not be so large, bright, or opaque that they completely hide the battlefield.

The goal is to create spectacular abilities without sacrificing gameplay clarity.

Performance and multiplayer considerations

Because this is a multiplayer PvP project, performance is extremely important

Experience with Nanos World, Garry’s Mod, Unreal Engine projects, or similar multiplayer game modes is a strong advantage.

The project is intended to grow over time, so a long-term collaboration may be possible if the quality, communication, and workflow are a good fit.

Busco un especialista en TikTok Ads Manager para e-commerce/dropshipping que pueda realizar una auditoría completa de mi cuenta publicitaria.

Mi negocio funciona bajo modalidad de dropshipping en Ecuador, principalmente en los nichos de perfumes y relojes. La publicidad de TikTok genera prospectos y las ventas se cierran principalmente por WhatsApp de forma manual; no dependo de que el cliente complete directamente una compra en Shopify.

El problema es que anteriormente TikTok Ads me daba mejores resultados, pero actualmente estamos recibiendo una cantidad muy alta de mensajes con una conversión demasiado baja. Como referencia, podemos recibir alrededor de 300 conversaciones y terminar con solo unas 5 ventas, por lo que necesito identificar qué está fallando.

Quiero revisar:

estructura de campañas y grupos de anuncios;
objetivo de campaña y optimización;
segmentación y calidad de los prospectos;
presupuestos, pujas y métricas;
creativos y anuncios utilizados;
costo por conversación y calidad de los mensajes recibidos;
posibles razones por las que llegan muchos prospectos pero pocos compradores;
estrategia recomendada para volver a testear y escalar.

También quiero determinar si el problema realmente está en TikTok Ads Manager, en la calidad del tráfico o en otra parte del embudo TikTok → WhatsApp → cierre de venta.

Busco inicialmente una auditoría puntual, idealmente mediante videollamada compartiendo pantalla y con un plan de acción concreto al finalizar.

Se valorará especialmente experiencia con TikTok Ads, dropshipping, ventas por WhatsApp, productos físicos, pago contra entrega y mercados de Latinoamérica.

En tu propuesta indícame brevemente:

Tu experiencia con TikTok Ads para e-commerce/dropshipping.
Qué revisarías primero en este caso.
Qué incluiría tu auditoría.
Precio y tiempo estimado.
Si puedes compartir evidencia o casos anteriores de tu trabajo.

URGENT – Magento 2 Security Incident Response / Malware Forensics / AWS

We require an experienced Magento 2 / Adobe Commerce security specialist for an urgent production incident.

Environment:

Magento 2.4.3-p1
PHP 7.4
AWS EC2
Cloudflare
~30,000 products

We have confirmed malicious JavaScript activity in production, including requests to:

d.digsgogo.com

and evidence of a suspicious checkout form submitting to:

s.setpayto.pw

Checkout has currently been restricted for customer protection.

We need someone who can urgently:

recover/establish secure SSH access through our AWS account if necessary;
preserve forensic evidence before cleanup;
identify the initial compromise and persistence mechanism;
inspect Magento files, generated/static content, database/configuration, cron jobs, Admin/API access and server logs;
identify all malicious files/code/configuration;
clean the environment safely;
rotate/revoke compromised access;
harden Magento/server/Cloudflare;
validate that checkout and storefront are clean before reopening;
investigate recurring OOM/Varnish/PHP/MySQL/Elasticsearch performance incidents;
provide a written technical report with findings, root cause and remediation.

We are not looking for someone who simply deletes infected generated files or runs an antivirus scan. Root-cause and persistence analysis are mandatory.

Please apply only if you have significant Magento 2 security/incident-response experience. Adobe Commerce/Magento certification, AWS experience and previous malware/card-skimmer investigations are strongly preferred.

In your proposal, please provide:

relevant Magento certifications;
examples of similar Magento compromise investigations;
AWS/Linux security experience;
your immediate availability;
your proposed first steps before making any changes to production.

I am specifically looking for a verified current employee of Google, Amazon, Shopify, Meta, Microsoft, Uber, Airbnb, TikTok, or a comparable global technology company.

The ideal professional currently works as a recruiter, hiring manager, talent acquisition specialist, product leader, category/vendor manager, marketplace leader, business operations manager, or another employee involved in evaluating, interviewing, hiring, managing, or referring candidates.

This is not a general resume-writing project. I need someone with direct, current, and verifiable Big Tech experience who understands internal candidate evaluation and can help me build a competitive application profile.

TARGET ROLES

* Category Manager / Vendor Manager
* E-commerce Manager / Marketplace Manager
* AI Product Builder / Product Manager
* Product Operations
* Business Operations / Program Manager

MY BACKGROUND

I have more than seven years of hands-on e-commerce and marketplace experience across the United States, Germany, and the United Kingdom.

My experience includes:

* Private Label, Wholesale, Online Arbitrage, and Dropshipping;
* Product research and selection;
* Supplier sourcing, evaluation, communication, and negotiation;
* Pricing, margin, cost, and profitability analysis;
* Inventory, orders, fulfillment, returns, and customer issues;
* Coordinating international suppliers, preparation centers, fulfillment partners, and external collaborators;
* More than €100,000 in cumulative revenue generated through my own business activities;
* Working with major international and European e-commerce platforms;
* Using data, customer feedback, competitor research, and commercial metrics to guide decisions;
* Improving workflows through milestones, clear deliverables, and review stages;
* Coordinating freelancers and influencing collaborators without direct managerial authority.

During the last two years, I have also built digital and AI-powered products. This experience includes:

* Transforming business ideas into functional products and MVPs;
* Market and competitor research;
* Defining customer problems, product requirements, user flows, and feature priorities;
* Prioritizing essential functionality and faster MVP launches;
* Coordinating designers, developers, and other freelancers;
* Working with APIs, payment systems, external services, automation, and AI tools at a product level;
* Testing integrations, identifying problems, and coordinating solutions;
* Building prototypes with modern AI-assisted tools;
* Improving products through testing, data, and feedback.

Some products and business information are confidential. Relevant metrics, screenshots, and case studies can be shared privately after identity and employment verification.

PROJECT OBJECTIVES

I need someone who can:

* Evaluate my professional background and determine the roles and seniority levels for which I am realistically qualified;
* Explain how my profile would be assessed internally;
* Translate my entrepreneurial experience into credible corporate language;
* Identify gaps, risks, and possible recruiter objections;
* Position my Category/E-commerce and AI Product experience separately;
* Build my complete application package;
* Develop an application and networking strategy;
* Explain the legitimate internal referral process;
* Identify suitable current openings where possible;
* Consider supporting my candidacy through legitimate internal channels if, after evaluating my profile, you believe I am qualified and your employer’s policies allow it.

I understand that no professional can guarantee a hiring decision. I want a verified current Big Tech employee who can strengthen my profile, explain the internal process, and, where appropriate, consider supporting my candidacy through legitimate company channels.

REQUIRED DELIVERABLES

1. Candidate and career evaluation

* Review my experience, projects, achievements, and metrics;
* Identify the strongest and weakest parts of my profile;
* Recommend suitable roles, companies, and seniority levels;
* Explain how to address recruiter objections honestly;
* Advise whether I should prioritize international remote employment, B2B work through my Romanian company, Employer of Record arrangements, or relocation.

2. Two ATS-friendly English resumes

Resume A:

Category Manager / Vendor Manager / E-commerce Manager / Marketplace Manager / Business Operations

Resume B:

AI Product Builder / Product Manager / Product Operations

Both resumes must:

* Be no longer than two pages;
* Use a clean ATS-compatible structure;
* Include truthful and relevant keywords;
* Present measurable results and commercial impact;
* Position entrepreneurship as relevant professional experience;
* Avoid invented experience or inflated titles;
* Be suitable for Big Tech and comparable companies;
* Be easy to adapt to specific job descriptions.

3. Complete LinkedIn optimization

* Headline;
* About section;
* Experience and project descriptions;
* Skills and Featured sections;
* Positioning for both Category/E-commerce and AI Product opportunities;
* Recruiter search and profile visibility recommendations;
* Guidance on presenting confidential projects safely.

4. Portfolio and case-study strategy

* Recommend which projects should be public or confidential;
* Structure three to five case studies;
* Explain how to present the problem, my role, decisions, execution, metrics, and results;
* Recommend suitable screenshots and commercial evidence after sensitive information is removed;
* Advise how to support older marketplace experience when the original accounts are no longer accessible.

5. Application strategy and materials

* One concise cover letter template;
* Recruiter outreach message;
* Employee networking message;
* Post-application follow-up message;
* Networking and application strategy;
* Guidance on requesting a legitimate internal referral;
* Instructions for adapting each resume to individual job descriptions;
* ATS recommendations without misleading claims or manipulation;
* A prioritized application plan.

6. Interview guidance

* Simulate an initial recruiter screening;
* Explain the likely interview process;
* Identify key behavioral, product, category, and operations questions;
* Advise how to present my transition from entrepreneurship to corporate work;
* Help address questions about my English, education, non-traditional experience, and lack of traditional corporate titles;
* Recommend the case studies and metrics required for interviews.

MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS

* You must currently work for a recognized Big Tech or comparable global technology company;
* Your identity and current employment must be verifiable;
* You must have relevant experience in recruitment, hiring, interviewing, management, Product, Category, Vendor, Marketplace, E-commerce, or Business Operations;
* You must understand how entrepreneurial candidates are assessed;
* You must have excellent professional English;
* You must maintain strict confidentiality;
* You must not fabricate qualifications, experience, metrics, or technical abilities;
* You must not use hidden text, misleading keyword stuffing, or unethical ATS techniques.

PROPOSAL REQUIREMENTS

Begin your proposal with:

Current company:
Current role:
Employment period:
Relevant hiring, interviewing, management, or candidate-evaluation experience:

Also include:

1. Your public LinkedIn profile;
2. The roles you have personally recruited for, interviewed, evaluated, managed, referred, or worked closely with;
3. Your experience with Product, Category, Vendor, Marketplace, E-commerce, or Business Operations candidates;
4. Anonymized examples you are authorized to share;
5. How you would position seven years of entrepreneurial e-commerce experience for Big Tech;
6. Your process and proposed milestones;
7. Exact deliverables and completion time;
8. Total fixed price;
9. The information and evidence you will need from me.

VERIFICATION

Shortlisted candidates must:

* Attend a short video call;
* Verify their identity and current employment appropriately;
* Provide a LinkedIn profile with consistent employment history;
* Explain their relevant experience using specific examples;
* Complete an initial paid evaluation milestone before starting the full project.

Verification must not involve sharing confidential employer information, internal systems, candidate data, or restricted documents.

Generic proposals, unverifiable employment claims, copied responses, and requests for communication or payment outside the platform will not be considered.

Please do not apply if you are only a general resume writer without current, verifiable experience inside a major global technology company.

I’m putting together an NLP-driven product and need a hands-on developer who works comfortably in Python and prefers PyTorch as the framework of choice. The immediate goal is to design, train, and fine-tune language models that will power features such as text classification, entity extraction, and semantic search.

You should be able to:  
• architect and code end-to-end pipelines—data ingestion, preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and deployment;  
• experiment with state-of-the-art transformer architectures, optimise hyperparameters, and benchmark performance on agreed metrics;  
• containerise and push models to a cloud endpoint (AWS, GCP, or Azure—choose what you know best);  
• document the approach clearly so the team can reproduce and extend your work.

Acceptance criteria for each milestone will include clean, well-commented Python code, reproducible training scripts in PyTorch, concise evaluation reports, and a working API endpoint exposing the chosen NLP task.

If this aligns with your expertise, let’s discuss timelines and the first deliverable.

I need a precise Plaxis 3D model that captures soil-structure interaction for a tunnel driven entirely through clay. The core objective is to simulate how the lining, excavation sequence and surrounding ground mutually influence one another, giving me reliable predictions of deformation, lining forces and surface settlement.  

You will receive bore-log data, in-situ test results and an outline of the tunnel geometry, construction stages and support details. From these inputs I expect you to:  
• build the full 3D geometry, apply appropriate boundary conditions and assign constitutive models that reflect soft to stiff clay behaviour;  
• stage the excavation and support exactly as specified so we can study time-dependent ground response;  
• run sensitivity checks on key parameters I highlight (e.g., undrained shear strength, creep) to bracket realistic outcomes;  
• export plots, graphs and a short explanatory memo that summarises displacements, bending moments, and any critical safety factors.  

Please send back the .p3d file, screenshots of the final mesh, and a concise PDF report so I can reproduce or tweak the analysis later. If you typically rely on UDSMs or have experience calibrating Hardening Soil or Soft Soil Creep models, let me know so we can incorporate those straight away.

# Independent WordPress Plugin Vulnerability Review

I am looking for an experienced WordPress security researcher / application security specialist to independently review a vulnerability finding in a WordPress plugin.

The finding has already been researched and documented against a recent plugin version. There is also a previously published vulnerability affecting earlier versions of the same plugin.

The objective is to determine whether our finding represents:

* a duplicate of the previously disclosed vulnerability;
* an incomplete fix or regression in the newer version;
* a technically distinct vulnerability variant;
* or an inconclusive result requiring additional evidence.

## Scope

The selected researcher will receive:

* our current vulnerability report;
* exact plugin version tested;
* HTTP request/response evidence;
* screenshots;
* reproduction notes;
* negative controls;
* relevant source-code observations;
* the public vulnerability disclosure for comparison.

The review should compare:

* affected version(s);
* vulnerable endpoint / route;
* parameters involved;
* authentication and authorization requirements;
* attacker preconditions;
* exploitation flow;
* security impact;
* HTTP evidence;
* screenshots and supporting artifacts;
* negative controls;
* differences from the previously disclosed vulnerability.

## Important restriction

This is a **documentary and technical review only**.

No testing against third-party websites, production systems, or external targets is required or authorized.

Any validation should be limited to the supplied evidence, source code, and/or a local controlled environment if necessary.

## Deliverable

A concise technical assessment containing:

1. Final verdict:

   * Duplicate
   * Incomplete fix / regression
   * Distinct variant
   * Inconclusive

2. Confidence level.

3. Evidence supporting the conclusion.

4. Evidence against the conclusion.

5. Identification of any missing evidence.

6. Recommended corrections or improvements to the vulnerability report before submission to a vulnerability disclosure program.

## Preferred experience

Strong experience with:

* WordPress plugin security;
* PHP application security;
* authentication / authorization vulnerabilities;
* REST and AJAX endpoint analysis;
* vulnerability disclosure programs;
* Patchstack, Wordfence, WPScan, CVE research, or similar ecosystems.

Experience independently validating vulnerability reports is especially valuable.

Please briefly describe previous WordPress vulnerability research or CVE / responsible disclosure experience when applying.

